{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Snowplow","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Snowplow"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for a Snowplow pipeline in one call. It checks the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collector’s URL, the Iglu vendor and the app ID, and posts to the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch to the limits of Snowplow’s own mobile trackers ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): 25"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events and 40,000 bytes a request, with a larger event, of up to 150,000 bytes, in a request of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collector takes events from anyone who can reach it, so there is no key or secret, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination builds on every platform: an app sends to the collector directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SnowplowEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ the Iglu vendor the plan is exported under","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: snowplow)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":" for a collector URL that isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":", that has no host,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a user name, a query or a fragment, or that already ends in the endpoint; for a vendor Iglu"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t take; and for an empty app ID or one longer than 255 UTF-16 code units."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Schemas-from-the-tracking-plan","text":"Schemas from the tracking plan","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each event is a self-describing event: its data comes with the Iglu URI of the schema it must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match, and Snowplow’s pipeline validates it against that schema before loading it. The URI is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named after the event and its version, under the vendor the destination is given:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Version N of an event is SchemaVer ","type":"text"},{"code":"N-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and events always name it. Raising an event’s version","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a breaking change, which is SchemaVer’s MODEL. The export compares each event with the newest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schema of its version the registry holds, by what the two mean rather than their bytes, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan’s own check does:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that hasn’t changed keeps its published file, and nothing is written."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A breaking change at the same version, such as a property made required, is refused: raise the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s version.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A compatible change, such as an optional property added, is an ADDITION. For Iglu Server the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"export writes it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"type":"text","text":", then "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-2"},{"type":"text","text":", each listing the earlier ones in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$supersedes"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow validates events naming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" against the newest, so a release already in users’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hands keeps validating. Superseding needs Iglu Server 0.11.0 or later and Enrich 3.8.0 or later."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A static repository doesn’t support it: it would validate those events against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" alone,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so for one the export refuses the change, and the event needs a new version."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the registry from the plan with "},{"code":"TrackingPlan.writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"iglu <vendor> server|static <registry-directory>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" command of the tracking plan’s executable, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"export-tracking-plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin’s "},{"code":"--iglu-vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"--iglu-registry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Then publish it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"igluctl","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before the release that sends the events."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event name Iglu takes holds only ASCII letters, digits, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":", and the version must be 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or more. The encoder skips every record of an event that breaks either rule, and logs a notice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each such event of the plan when the destination is made. The export refuses such an event too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-Snowplow-receives","text":"What Snowplow receives","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"payload_data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" 1-0-4 array of events, one per record. Every event has:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a self-describing event, with its data in ","type":"text"},{"code":"ue_pr","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as JSON text;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in milliseconds, so Snowplow’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the event was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the app ID; "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform; "},{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; and "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"stm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, when the record has it, goes in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"},{"text":" as Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile_context"},{"text":" 1-0-3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the operating system, Apple as the manufacturer, the device model, the network type and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application"},{"text":" 1-0-0 (the app’s version and build). The platform is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"text":" for a phone,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pad, watch or Vision Pro, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"text":" for an Apple TV, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"text":" for a Mac and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"text":" for a record with no device.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Only-the-session-identifies-a-record","text":"Only the session identifies a record","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, from the sessions enricher, is its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"text":", Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"domain_sessionid"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else identifies it. No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duid"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uid"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nuid"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tnuid"},{"text":" is sent, no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entity (its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"text":" lasts across sessions), and no IDFV, IDFA or other device identifier. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent either. A record with no session, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one a store recovered after a relaunch, is sent without a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"text":". Snowplow’s mobile data models","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read a session from the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_session"},{"text":" entity, so set the unified package’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"snowplow__session_identifiers"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[{\"schema\": \"atomic\", \"field\": \"domain_sessionid\"}]"},{"text":" for these","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The collector would give each device an identifier of its own: it sets an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sp"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps and sends back, and records the request’s IP address. Every request carries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SP-Anonymous: *"},{"type":"text","text":", so the collector sets and reads no cookie, records "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network_userid"},{"type":"text","text":" as all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zeros, and records no IP address or forwarding header fields."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose event name Iglu doesn’t take, or whose version is below 1;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 0 to 9999, which Snowplow’s enrichment fails;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes, which the smallest of a pipeline’s streams, SQS’s 192 kB,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"might not take with the request around it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-the-collector-doesnt-report","text":"What the collector doesn’t report","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The collector answers 200 to every request it can read and validates nothing. Snowplow checks the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events later, in enrichment. An event whose data its schema rejects, whose schema the pipeline’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, or that is larger than the pipeline’s stream takes, becomes a failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event: it is kept apart and never reaches the warehouse, though the destination counted it as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered. Publish each schema before the release that sends it, and watch the pipeline’s failed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events after a change to the plan. Snowplow’s resolver caches schemas, for 10 minutes by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a schema published after the first event that names it can still be missed for that long.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow doesn’t remove duplicates as events arrive. A record is sent more than once when a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is retried after the collector stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each copy keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s data models, which deduplicate on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_id"},{"type":"text","text":", count it once."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Snowplow receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"SnowplowEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"SnowplowEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder","title":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Snowplow’s tracker protocol, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can send events to a Snowplow collector’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/tp2","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-describing events whose schemas are the tracking plan’s.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowEncodingError":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowencodingerror","title":"SnowplowEncodingError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnowplowEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appid:plan:backoff:clock:)","title":"snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Snowplow collector at "},{"code":"collector","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as self-describing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events whose schemas are "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s under "},{"code":"vendor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", from the app "},{"code":"appID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"code":"backoff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"clock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"snowplow"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"collector"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"vendor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","text":"Clock"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A10SetupErrorO","text":"Snow